WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:03.750
Welcome! In this second part

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:08.460
of decision making without probabilities,
we will be discussing the

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.509
Equally-Likely approach and we'll also be discussing

00:00:12.509 --> 00:00:17.060
the Realism approach. We will be using

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:20.080
this Payoff table and assume

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:26.650
payoffs are profits. The equally likely

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:31.750
or Laplace approach. Using this approach
we choose the alternative

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:36.489
with the best average payoff. To find the
average payoff

00:00:36.489 --> 00:00:41.829
we add the payoffs in a decision alternative and divide the total by the number of payoffs

00:00:41.829 --> 00:00:45.120
With bonds,

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.570
the average  payoff is 30. The average

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:52.840
is 29 for stocks, and the average

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:57.030
is 31 for Mutual Funds. The best of these

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:01.660
is 31. Therefore the equally likely
decision

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:10.100
is to invest in Mutual Funds.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:13.460
The Realism or Hurwicz
approach.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:17.620
This approach find a compromise between the best

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:21.960
and worst payoffs. Using this approach we choose the alternative

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.190
with the best weighted average payoff based

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:29.500
on the coefficient of realism α. The coefficient

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.900
of realism α is a value between
0 &amp; 1

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:38.510
determined by the decision maker. For each decision alternative,

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:42.229
the approach here is to multiply the best payoff by α

00:01:42.229 --> 00:01:46.229
multiplied the worst payoff

00:01:46.229 --> 00:01:50.310
by 1 minus α, and then add the two
results.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.729
Note that when of α close to 1

00:01:53.729 --> 00:01:58.660
decision-maker is optimistic, and when α is close 0

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:03.660
the decision maker is pessimistic. In
this example

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:07.210
we choose α equals 0.3.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:10.410
And thus, 1 minus α

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:15.890
is 0.7. This indicates that the decision-maker is leaning towards

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:19.730
pessimism. Let us now calculate the
weighted

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:24.130
average for each decision. For Bonds

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:27.840
the best payoff is 45 and the
worst is 5.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.170
So we calculate 0.3 times 45

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:35.340
plus 0.7 times 5

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:40.380
and the result is 17. For Stocks

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:44.269
the best payoff is 70 and the worst
is negative 13

00:02:44.269 --> 00:02:47.470
The weighted average

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:50.910
is .3 times 70 plus .7 times

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:54.680
-13 which gives 11.9

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:58.170
For Mutual Funds, the best payoff is 53

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:02.200
and the worst is -5. The weighted average

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:06.620
.3 times 53 plus .7 seven times -5

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:10.220
which equals 12.4. The best

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:15.360
of these is 17. Therefore the realism
approach

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:18.890
decision is to invest in bonds.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:22.010
In this video I have shown how to

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:23.140
make decisions

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:26.550
using the equally likely and realism
approaches.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:27.900
Thanks for watching!

